All checks pass. Summary of the change:

1. **Added `isResearchDomainTask(task)`** (line 153 of `src/local-draft.js`): returns `/^Research:/i.test((task && task.title || '').trim())`, matching the pre-model-call string-gate style of `detectExternalDependency`.
2. **Pre-check extended** (the `researchClaudeStatus` guard before `runPlanPass`): now `task.domain === 'research' || isResearchDomainTask(task)`, so an unopted/paused Claude still blocks cleanly for Research:-titled tasks.
3. **Early short-circuit added** right after that pre-check: `if (isResearchDomainTask(task)) return await draftResearchBranch(...)` — this fires **before** `runPlanPass` (plan-stage model call) and **before** the `resolveSourceName(task) === 'adhoc'` branch whose tier ladder would otherwise swallow a Research:-titled adhoc task. (The real code had the adhoc dispatch *before* the research dispatch, which the plan's assumption didn't account for — the actual structure won, hence the explicit early return.)
4. **Defence-in-depth OR** also added to the later `draftResearchBranch` dispatch condition (~line 2395).
5. `src/research-agentic-draft.js` and `src/local-agentic-write-draft.js` untouched; no test file changes.

